id: pm-m0b7h8
title: Linked-test removal must be lossless and observable for commands containing comma or equals delimiters
description: "GitHub #982 proves pm test --add-json can persist a command containing comma and equals characters that pm test --remove cannot later address. The remove selector is reparsed as structured CSV, silently matches nothing, and returns ok:true without a removed count. This creates stale evidence that cannot be repaired through the supported CLI. All-status exact and conjunctive searches for linked-test removal, delimiter-safe selectors, comma/equals commands, and no-op removal found no canonical owner."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[8]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",contracts,linked-tests,lossless-mutation,safety,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-08-11T20:50:17.622Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-11T22:24:04.466Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-11T22:24:03.826Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-11T22:24:03.826Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Every linked-test command accepted by --add or --add-json can be removed losslessly even when it contains comma or equals characters; Removal reports an explicit removed count and a zero-match selector never returns an indistinguishable success receipt; A stable index selector addresses the 1-based --list order without reparsing stored command text; CLI SDK MCP help contracts completions and docs expose one shared selector contract; Focused integration packaged npm npx bun bunx exact 100/100/100/100 coverage docstring and static gates pass
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make linked-test evidence fully reversible and make no-op mutations machine-observable
value: Agents can repair stale test evidence without hand-editing tracker files or trusting false-success receipts
impact: Linked-test mutation becomes lossless across CLI SDK and MCP consumers
why_now: The current published package can create evidence it cannot remove and silently reports success while leaving it stale
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: high
confidence: 98
reporter: GitHub #982
severity: high
environment: @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.7 through 2026.8.11 Node 22/26 Linux
repro_steps: "Add a linked test command name=x,result=pass with pm test --add-json then remove it by command value; observe ok:true and the entry remains"
resolution: "Linked-test removal now preserves delimiter-bearing commands, supports stable 1-based remove indexes, returns effective removed counts, and rejects zero matches with a typed not-found error."
expected_result: The exact entry is removed or the command returns a typed zero-match refusal with removed=0
actual_result: "The selector is split at delimiters no entry matches and the mutation reports ok:true with no observable removal count"
